<title>USA: CIBCR U.S. leading inflation index 105.9 in July.</title>
<headline>CIBCR U.S. leading inflation index 105.9 in July.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Center for International Business Cycle  Research (CIBCR) said its U.S. leading inflation index (LII) rose  to 105.9 in July from a revised 105.0 in June.</p>
<p>&quot;The mild upward drift in the LII would anticipate somewhat larger  rates of inflation than those recently observed in the U.S. comprehensive  price indexes, but the differences seem too small to warrant any danger  signal,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
